{
  "url": "/2026/06/18/2.-Subspaces.html",
  "title": "1.2 Subspaces",
  "lang": "en",
  "description": "Within a vector space, we often focus on elements that satisfy a particular condition. The important question is whether the condition survives the operations of the larger space: do addition and scalar multiplication keep us among elements satisfying that condition? If they do, and the zero vector also satisfies the condition, the collection forms a vector space on its own. Such a collection is called a subspace.",
  "published_at": "2026-06-18T15:00:00+00:00",
